    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">Linux / Fedora install notes</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">Field notes for Node lines, Ghidra+JDK, browsers, and Fedora-family host quirks.</p>
    <h2>Node</h2>
    <p>Match upstream’s supported Node lines (commonly 22.x / 24.x / 26+). Electron/JS targets are sensitive to that floor — do not assume system Node 18 is enough.</p>
    <h2>Ghidra + JDK</h2>
    <p>Pair a documented Ghidra release with a full Temurin (or equivalent) JDK 21+. Export <code>GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR</code> and <code>JAVA_HOME</code>, then <code>doctor --provider ghidra</code>.</p>
    <h2>Browser tools</h2>
    <p>If page inspection cannot find Chrome/Chromium, set <code>REA_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE</code> to an absolute binary. Some Chromium builds report opaque placeholder URLs in frame trees — upgrade REA/browser when frame discovery fails.</p>
    <h2>Host distros</h2>
    <p>Fedora-based spins (including Nobara) have been reported as <code>unsupported_host</code> in older builds; check whether your REA version still gates that way before filing duplicates. Optional reverse tooling (pwntools, etc.) belongs in its own venv — REA setup will not replace your distro packages.</p>
    <p>Also read <a href="/faq/tmpdir-dot-path/">TMPDIR pitfalls</a> on Linux temp layouts.</p>

        <h2 id="startup">Startup benchmarks (community)</h2>
    <p>Discussion <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/discussions/1998" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1998</a> published Node 22/24/26 tool-list and first-job timings for 6.3.0 / 6.4.0 / main on OSS fixtures. Headline: 6.4 lists more tools → list can be slower while Android scans improve. Full write-up: <a href="/blog/rea-linux-startup-benchmarks/">Linux startup benchmarks</a>.</p>

